1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,216
Welcome to Unit Four of Algebra Two:
complex numbers. We start with a new

2
00:00:05,216 --> 00:00:05,931
number, i.

3
00:00:07,067 --> 00:00:12,916
No real number squared gives negative one.
So x squared equals negative one has no

4
00:00:12,916 --> 00:00:13,915
real solution.

5
00:00:14,365 --> 00:00:17,479
Mathematicians invented a number to fill
that gap.

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:23,763
The imaginary unit i is defined so that i
squared equals negative one.

7
00:00:24,213 --> 00:00:27,541
In other words, i is the square root of
negative one.

8
00:00:28,667 --> 00:00:34,243
Now we can take square roots of negatives.
The square root of negative nine is the

9
00:00:34,243 --> 00:00:37,371
square root of nine times i, which is
three i.

10
00:00:37,821 --> 00:00:41,661
The square root of negative twelve is two
root three times i.

11
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:48,432
Powers of i repeat in a cycle of four: i,
negative one, negative i, one.

12
00:00:48,882 --> 00:00:54,252
To find i to the twenty-third, divide
twenty-three by four. The remainder is

13
00:00:54,252 --> 00:00:57,714
three, so it equals i cubed, which is
negative i.

14
00:00:58,833 --> 00:01:04,911
A complex number has the form a plus b i,
where a is the real part and b is the

15
00:01:04,911 --> 00:01:06,065
imaginary part.

16
00:01:06,515 --> 00:01:10,014
Every real number is complex, with b equal
to zero.

17
00:01:11,133 --> 00:01:15,848
Your turn. Simplify the square root of
negative fifty, and i to the tenth.

18
00:01:16,298 --> 00:01:17,834
Pause the video and try it.

19
00:01:18,284 --> 00:01:23,772
The square root of negative fifty is five
root two times i. i to the tenth has

20
00:01:23,772 --> 00:01:26,305
remainder two, so it's negative one.

21
00:01:27,433 --> 00:01:33,520
Complex numbers follow the same rules as
algebra, with one extra fact: i squared is

22
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:34,473
negative one.

23
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:40,122
To add or subtract, combine the real parts
and the imaginary parts.

24
00:01:40,572 --> 00:01:45,138
Three plus two i, plus one minus five i,
is four minus three i.

25
00:01:46,266 --> 00:01:49,338
To multiply, distribute, just like
binomials.

26
00:01:49,788 --> 00:01:55,896
Two plus three i, times four minus i, is
eight minus two i plus twelve i minus

27
00:01:55,896 --> 00:01:57,148
three i squared.

28
00:01:58,266 --> 00:02:03,664
Replace i squared with negative one: minus
three i squared becomes plus three.

29
00:02:04,114 --> 00:02:06,503
So the product is eleven plus ten i.

30
00:02:07,633 --> 00:02:10,854
Complex numbers can be plotted in the
complex plane.

31
00:02:11,304 --> 00:02:17,216
The real part goes on the horizontal axis,
and the imaginary part on the vertical

32
00:02:17,216 --> 00:02:21,011
axis. Three plus two i is the point three
comma two.

33
00:02:22,133 --> 00:02:27,566
Careful: the square root of negative four
times the square root of negative nine is

34
00:02:27,566 --> 00:02:29,792
not the square root of thirty-six.

35
00:02:30,242 --> 00:02:35,939
Write them as two i and three i first.
Their product is six i squared, which is

36
00:02:35,939 --> 00:02:36,876
negative six.

37
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,840
Your turn. Multiply one plus two i by
three minus i.

38
00:02:42,290 --> 00:02:43,826
Pause the video and try it.

39
00:02:44,276 --> 00:02:49,609
Three minus i plus six i minus two i
squared. That's five plus five i.

40
00:02:50,733 --> 00:02:55,661
Dividing by a complex number needs a
special partner, called the conjugate.

41
00:02:56,800 --> 00:03:03,299
The conjugate of a plus b i is a minus b
i. You just flip the sign of the imaginary

42
00:03:03,299 --> 00:03:03,690
part.

43
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:08,236
The conjugate of three plus four i is
three minus four i.

44
00:03:09,366 --> 00:03:13,953
Multiplying a number by its conjugate
always gives a real number.

45
00:03:14,403 --> 00:03:20,857
Three plus four i times three minus four i
is nine minus sixteen i squared, which is

46
00:03:20,857 --> 00:03:23,470
nine plus sixteen, or twenty-five.

47
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:29,826
To divide, multiply the top and bottom by
the conjugate of the denominator.

48
00:03:30,276 --> 00:03:36,335
Two plus i, over three minus i: multiply
by three plus i over three plus i.

49
00:03:36,785 --> 00:03:42,669
The top becomes six plus five i plus i
squared, which is five plus five i. The

50
00:03:42,669 --> 00:03:44,102
bottom becomes ten.

51
00:03:45,233 --> 00:03:47,836
So the answer is one half plus one half i.

52
00:03:48,286 --> 00:03:54,602
Here's another: five over two i. Multiply
by negative i over negative i to get

53
00:03:54,602 --> 00:03:56,627
negative five i over two.

54
00:03:57,766 --> 00:04:02,972
Always write the answer in a plus b i
form, with no i in the denominator.

55
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:07,598
Your turn. Divide four plus two i by one
plus i.

56
00:04:08,048 --> 00:04:09,584
Pause the video and try it.

57
00:04:10,034 --> 00:04:16,288
Multiply by one minus i. The top is four
minus four i plus two i minus two i

58
00:04:16,288 --> 00:04:22,130
squared, which is six minus two i. The
bottom is two. So three minus i.

59
00:04:23,266 --> 00:04:28,410
Now every quadratic equation has
solutions. In this last lesson of Unit

60
00:04:28,410 --> 00:04:30,583
Four, we'll find complex ones.

61
00:04:31,733 --> 00:04:35,850
When the discriminant is negative, the
parabola misses the x axis.

62
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:39,799
There are no real solutions, but there are
two complex ones.

63
00:04:40,933 --> 00:04:44,581
Solve x squared minus two x plus five
equals zero.

64
00:04:45,031 --> 00:04:50,708
The discriminant is four minus twenty,
which is negative sixteen. Its square root

65
00:04:50,708 --> 00:04:51,409
is four i.

66
00:04:51,859 --> 00:04:58,899
So x equals two plus or minus four i, over
two: one plus two i, or one minus two i.

67
00:05:00,033 --> 00:05:05,783
Notice the solutions are conjugates.
Complex solutions of real quadratics

68
00:05:05,783 --> 00:05:08,225
always come in conjugate pairs.

69
00:05:09,366 --> 00:05:14,635
Without an x term, use square roots. x
squared plus forty-nine equals zero.

70
00:05:15,085 --> 00:05:20,269
x squared is negative forty-nine, so x
equals plus or minus seven i.

71
00:05:21,399 --> 00:05:24,386
Check one plus two i in the original
equation.

72
00:05:24,836 --> 00:05:31,200
Its square is negative three plus four i.
Then negative three plus four i, minus two

73
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:34,457
minus four i, plus five, is zero. It
works.

74
00:05:35,599 --> 00:05:40,165
Your turn. Solve x squared plus four x
plus thirteen equals zero.

75
00:05:40,615 --> 00:05:42,151
Pause the video and try it.

76
00:05:42,601 --> 00:05:48,546
The discriminant is sixteen minus
fifty-two, which is negative thirty-six. x

77
00:05:48,546 --> 00:05:55,116
equals negative four plus or minus six i,
over two: negative two plus or minus three

78
00:05:55,116 --> 00:05:55,273
i.

79
00:05:56,399 --> 00:06:01,565
That completes Unit Four. Next, we'll
study polynomial functions in Unit Five.

80
00:06:01,565 --> 00:06:06,929
If this helped, subscribe to School Math,
Explained, and turn on notifications so

81
00:06:06,929 --> 00:06:09,114
you don't miss it. See you there.

